<title>POLAND: BPH wins tender to lend Warsaw PLN 88 mln.</title>
<headline>BPH wins tender to lend Warsaw PLN 88 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy SA (BPH) won a tender to lend the city of Warsaw 88 million zlotys over eight years for the purchase of buses and trams, the bank's spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;BPH has won the tender (announced by the Warsaw authorities). A contract will soon be signed,&quot; Andrzej Charlemagne told Reuters, adding that five banks had participated in the tender.</p>
<p>He said the interest rate would be based on the average WIBOR rate from the previous quarter.</p>
<p>The money will go toward the purchase of 180 buses and several dozen trams. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
